      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Encryption Provider**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google Cloud KMS as the managed key service for encrypting the payload. I'm focusing now on how to cleanly integrate the provider's specifics into the `encrypt_payload.py` file to keep the code organized and easily maintainable.\n\n\n**Implementing KMS Encryption**\n\nI'm now integrating the Google Cloud KMS client within `encrypt_payload.py`. I'm structuring the code to include a specific `encrypt_payload` function that accepts parameters for project, location, key ring, key ID, and the plaintext itself. I am aiming to use the client to encrypt the plaintext and returning the resulting ciphertext.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789861699970,
          "start": 1789861698660
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc121c64001kG8CyIhGU14vc7",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc1217ab001bbE3sf0i3pnZWy",
      "session_id": "ses_f43ede8e0ffeNMDYkWhR9B4uRh",
      "time_created": 1789861698660,
      "time_updated": 1789861699970
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "87GFkwVNBDGm24j0",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import kms_v1\n\ndef encrypt_payload(project_id: str, location_id: str, key_ring_id: str, key_id: str, plaintext: bytes) -> bytes:\n    \"\"\"\n    Encrypts a plaintext payload with a managed key using Google Cloud KMS.\n    \"\"\"\n    client = kms_v1.KeyManagementServiceClient()\n    name = client.crypto_key_path(project_id, location_id, key_ring_id, key_id)\n    response = client.encrypt(name=name, plaintext=plaintext)\n    return response.ciphertext\n",
            "filePath": "encrypt_payload.py"
          },
